# Pressure methods v4 · v4-gcr CUDA

Retrospective source review · fit-6a1cb8a085cb73f0

Authored interpretation of captured source and receipts. No new training, benchmark, lineage or scientific promotion is implied.

**Method.** A 371,214-parameter F32 pressure proposal has 370,016 fine CNN coefficients at widths 8/16/24/32, bottleneck 48, 63 learned positive low-mode gains and a 1,135-parameter 3→16 tanh→63 grid-shape head. The fine path is linear and bias-free, with pooling, nearest upsampling, skips and global-mean broadcast. Its input is q=(rho/h)r normalized by fixed original C53 scales; dt is validated scalar metadata, not an independent neural channel. At each correction the learned cosine coarse proposal is gated by its actual F64 fine-equation residual, followed by a neural correction accumulated in F64. Deployment performs two flexible GCR iterations with two reorthogonalization sweeps, image normalization and a recomputed true residual after each update. No analytic coarse inverse supplies the learned proposal.

**Purpose.** Train and deploy two flexible GCR iterations using the learned pressure proposal, comparing solver-aware training and inference with the ordinary two-correction C108 control.

**Experiment.** 2,400 CUDA Adam updates, batch one, clip norm one. Fine rate 1e-05; executed optimizer multipliers [1.0, 1000.0]. Every update uses one recorded physical request: 1,600 preserved small-grid samples plus 800 round-robin size-tier samples. There are 34 train-only parents and 68 selected frames, fixed dt=1/60 s and fluid density 1,000 kg/m³. Actual parent grid resolutions: {'8.0': 15, '16.0': 17, '32.0': 2}; sample tier exposures: {'16': 1600, '32': 267, '64': 267, '128': 266}. Actual fine-network work is 4,800 root forwards / 1,224,395,120 input voxels. Inherited manufactured, direction and current-policy banks are disabled despite retained config labels. Final/intermediate physical equation feedback remains, with early log-residual weight 0.05 and target 1e-6. The old eight-pass teacher has weight zero. GCR is differentiated during training and used at publication/deployment. Its log-residual denominator combines target scaling before clamping to avoid the historical overflow derivative. 

**Observed outcome.** Final retained weighted training loss 17.9176192787288. On the common 128 original consumed requests, worst mean-free pressure relative L2 is 0.0038993858106244014, equation relative L2 0.00051156346950678364. Retained complete GPU pressure-call median of case medians is 7.9175509999999996 ms, with CPU input/output, validation/packing, transfers, all solver work and synchronization included. Setup and scoring are separate. The native training diagnostic named validation is train-only, and the wrapper probe is already consumed. The common test covers small 8/16-cells-per-metre grids, not the larger training domains. No fresh forward, latency, trajectory or held-out result is added by this review.

**Lesson.** GCR improves both common pressure and equation tails over C108, with higher complete pressure-call GPU latency. It changes the training unroll and deployed solver work together, including residual actions, reductions and double orthogonalization; this is not an architecture-only or loss-only intervention.

**Reproduction.** Use the exact captured native evidence recipe, all witnessed sources/configuration, runtime, fixed normalization, typed input packet, initial parameter inventory and final-update checkpoint. Preserve the private small/large RNG streams and physical exposure budget, disabled auxiliary banks and executed optimizer groups. Retain channel-slice mappings or exact warm-parent bytes, and distinguish teacher work from student work. Original CPU publication/restore performs neural inference and must be replaced by a qualified GPU-only route before replay. Native recipe rebuilding, clean retraining, new-Rheon regeneration and own-history drift remain unqualified; historical Trial ancestry is unchanged.

